- PUT-replace-variables contract suite on a bare-{id}-resolver route (BE-0175 contract pattern, internal/controlplane/httpapi/environment_variables_put_test.go): canonical 12-test contract suite for ANY customer-facing PUT-replace-{secret-bearing-children} endpoint sitting on a bare-{id}-resolver route. Structural HYBRID of (a) environment_grants_put_test.go (BE-0169 contract pattern — route-shape twin: same env-id resolver, same NewHandler positional port placement, same missing-field-400 + malformed-400 + unknown-field-400 + unauth-401 + viewer-403 + store NotFound 404 + store InvalidInput 400 + store unavailable 503 + unwired 500 + OpenAPI registration skeleton) and (b) project_variables_test.go (BE-0142 GET pattern — resource-shape twin: output.Sentinel projection of is_secret rows, secret-plaintext leak guards on response bodies including the seeded substring). The pattern adds TWO load-bearing assertions BE-0169 (a grants-only resource) cannot supply: (1) the happy-path body POSITIVELY asserts got0.Value == output.Sentinel for the secret row AND negatively asserts the body does not contain the seeded plaintext — the wire chokepoint must fire on the post-write re-read even though the caller just submitted the plaintext; both directions catch different regressions. (2) A dedicated TestDeniesSupportInTenant — CapWrite has no support exception (the CapRead cross-tenant exception is one-way), so a CapWrite contract suite MUST positively assert support in their own tenant is denied 403, locking the deny against a future engine regression that widens CapWrite to support. apierr.InvalidInput wire shape: the renderer emits FieldViolation as "<field>: <reason>" inside the hint, NOT as a JSON key with quotes — a contract test that asserts the field path reaches the wire must use the substring "variables: " (with space), NOT "variables" wrapped in double-quotes; the success envelope DOES use "variables" as a JSON key but the error envelope serialises the field path into a