diff --git a/ralph/progress.txt b/ralph/progress.txt
index aa24c03b11d0ab3d59432b4280264e7ee6109085..b40dacc1510701031d7e6b676c255ced76d7e2c2
--- a/ralph/progress.txt
+++ b/ralph/progress.txt
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 ## Codebase Patterns
+- Worker queue metrics follow the HTTP metrics collector shape: aggregate series by low-cardinality dimensions only (`event`, `job_type`, `status`, `status_class`), keep job/request/correlation/org/project/environment/service identifiers as latest-sample log-join hints, and emit worker events only after successful claim/outcome commits so metrics reflect durable queue state.
 - Billing-grade container metric stories follow the same four-piece tracked-metric vertical as Traefik/build metering: add a runtime `metering.MetricDefinition`, extend the closed `quota_resource` domain plus `store.QuotaResource`, quarantine samples before billing unless attribution resolves a full org/project/environment/service scope, and emit idempotent `usage_events` whose current-period aggregation is visible through the organization usage projection.
 - HTTP request metrics live in `internal/controlplane/telemetry` and are wired by `httpapi.NewHandler` inside request logging: group metric series only by method, normalized route, status code, and status class; keep request/correlation/org/principal identifiers as latest-sample log-join hints instead of dashboard labels.
 - Billing-grade Traefik metric stories should add four pieces together: a runtime `metering.MetricDefinition`, a new `quota_resource` migration + `store.QuotaResource` constant when the key is invoiceable, an idempotent emitter that writes only fully attributed samples into `usage_events`, and a customer usage projection from current-period `usage_counters`.
@@ -218,6 +219,7 @@
 - PATCH endpoint for a deep resource by bare id (BE-0157 pattern, PATCH /v1/environments/{environment_id}, store/environment.go EnvironmentRepository.Update + classifyEnvironmentConcurrencyMiss, store/environmentservice.go EnvironmentService.Update + buildEnvironmentUpdate, httpapi/environments.go updateEnvironmentHandler): canonical shape for ALL deep-resource PATCH endpoints. Repository.Update takes a fully-formed row + *int64 ifMatchVersion, runs a tenant-scoped (organization_id, id) UPDATE that touches only the mutable columns (slug, display_name — NEVER the composite tenant key), and classifies a zero-row return via a classify*ConcurrencyMiss helper that disambiguates gone-vs-stale by Get-in-same-tx. The service-layer orchestrator runs the validation BEFORE the transaction is opened (buildXxxUpdate is split out for unit-testability, rejects empty patches as 400, never echoes submitted values in violations), then in ONE Store.Write: read current row, check If-Match pre-condition (stale -> ConflictStale with row's authoritative version BEFORE the version-checked UPDATE — even a trivial no-op patch with stale If-Match surfaces the conflict), apply patch in-memory, call Repository.Update, append audit row. UNLIKE Create, the orchestrator does NOT invoke the in-tx Authorizer or QuotaReserver — the HTTP RequireAuth gate is authoritative for the update path; the in-tx Authorize is reserved for Create's defence-in-depth against grant-change races during quota reservation. The HTTP handler reuses the shared parseIfMatchVersion + writeOrganizationETag helpers (yes, the helper is org-named but it is the SHARED chokepoint for every endpoint mirroring versions to ETag — do not duplicate it per resource family). Body is strictly decoded with `slug *string` and `display_name *string` (pointer nil-ness IS the partial-update contract); the body intentionally exposes no organization_id/parent_id/self_id field — tenant isolation is structural. Response is yalla.output.v1 carrying the same wire shape GET returns, plus ETag header. Path with NO parent_id (bare-id route): the resource scope pins only OrganizationID + the deep id, so the engine's covers() rule DENIES every scoped grant at the policy boundary (a grant with a pinned ProjectID cannot cover a resource with no ProjectID); principals whose only access is a scoped grant must use a parent-scoped route. Every NewHandler positional-arg addition triggers a ~50-site sweep across ~35 existing test files — anchor on `fakeXxxReader{}, nil)` and `fakeXxxReader{}, logger)` plus the `reader, nil)` / `reader, logger)` outliers in the resource's own get/policy test helpers. The newRouteTable-only OpenAPI shape tests (all-nils form, partial-fakes-with-trailing-nils form) each need one more `nil` appended. AVOID double-counting: run go vet AFTER each automated sweep and undo overshoots before continuing.
